<title>HUNGARY: Hungary July PMI index 51.8 pct vs June's 56.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary July PMI index 51.8 pct vs June's 56.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Purchasing Manager Index (PMI) was 51.8 percent in July, down from 56.7 percent in June, the Hungarian Association of Logistics, Purchasing and Inventory Management (HALPIM) said on Monday.</p>
<p>The following is a history of the index on a month-to-month basis:</p>
<p>PURCHASING MANAGER INDEX (Percent)</p>
<p> 1997 July		     51.8</p>
<p>	June		     56.7</p>
<p>	May			53.3</p>
<p>	April		    58.0</p>
<p>	March		    55.1</p>
<p>	February		 50.4</p>
<p>	January		  46.0</p>
<p> 1996 December		 44.7</p>
<p>	November		 52.8</p>
<p>	October		  57.8</p>
<p>	September		60.4</p>
<p>	August		   52.7</p>
<p>	July		     48.5</p>
<p>NOTE: The PMI is calculated using the same methodology as the United States' National Association of Purchasing Management Index. A figure above 50 indicates increasing economic activity, while a number below 50 shows declining economic activity.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
</text>
